# DBUG1 - W35: a delete expression the exe runs through a scalar deleting wrapper. Method: docs/PATCHES.md.

@@ DBUG1 src/staging/blk_00660000_od.cpp 0x0066e200
# x86 0x0066e200 ends its loop with `push 1; call 0x004702f0` on the node: the scalar deleting wrapper, which runs the
# list destructor body (0x0046ffb0, one call to RemoveAll) and then, with bit 0 of its flag set, the unsized operator
# delete 0x00401030 on the node. The decomp's `delete (SaveNodeExtended*)` compiled by GCC runs the same destructor
# and then the global sized `operator delete(void*, unsigned)` of the unit (the game's 0x00aa1460, a different
# function: GCC takes the sized form as the usual deallocation, MSVC 2008 never does). GCC builds give the class the
# unsized deallocation the exe's wrapper calls; MSVC keeps the class as measured.
<<<
    ~SaveNodeExtended();
};
===
    ~SaveNodeExtended();
#ifndef _MSC_VER
    static void operator delete(void* p) { FUN_00401030(p); }
#endif
};
>>>
